{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1519309147,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyOTkzNzA3Nzc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2213","origin":"github"},"title":"export_to_figshare's annex check is always true","message":"The export_to_figshare plugin seems to make the same false assumption that I made about boolean flags in the plugin interface.\n\n```python\ndef dlplugin(dataset, filename=None,\n             missing_content='error',\n             annex=True,\n             # project_id=None,  # TODO: support working with projects and articles within them\n             article_id=None\n             ):\n    \"\"\"[...]\n    annex : bool, optional\n      If True generated .zip file would be added to annex, and all files\n      would get registered in git-annex to be available from such a tarball. Also\n      upon upload we will register for that archive to be a possible source for it\n      in annex.\n```\n\nAt least as a user, I'd assume that I could then pass `annex=False`.  This won't work, however, because the string 'False' is used as the value.  As a result, the `if annex:` check always evaluates to true.\n\n\nAs a simple example of the behavior\n\n```python\ndef dlplugin(dataset, false_flag=False, true_flag=True):\n    print(\"false_flag: {!r}\".format(false_flag))\n    print(\"true_flag: {!r}\".format(true_flag))\n```\n\nUnsupplied defaults are OK:\n\n```\n$ datalad plugin bool\nfalse_flag: False\ntrue_flag: True\n```\n\nNon-defaults are strings:\n\n```\n$ datalad plugin bool false_flag=True true_flag=False\nfalse_flag: 'True'\ntrue_flag: 'False'\n```","files":null}]}